From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 07:42:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 036/184] segacd: keep the Genesis off the bus during a CDD
 exchange

One command sent and then silence -- the same signature as the very
first hardware test, unchanged by every correction to the protocol.
That is a strong hint the protocol was never the problem.

The Genesis halts this CPU with SBRQ every frame to read the screen out
of PRG-RAM. A halt landing inside a CDD exchange does not delay it, it
destroys it: the gate array clocks a fixed exchange every 1/75 s and a
grab lasting milliseconds drops us out of that window. A status read
arriving late costs nothing, which is exactly why the passive link has
been flawless throughout; a command arriving late is corruption.

The sub now raises a flag for the few microseconds it is mid-exchange
and the servant honours it. Emulators cannot show this either way --
their arbitration is instant and neither models the transfer window.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 669baa0..e358576 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -325,6 +325,18 @@ void segacd_int_4_c(void)
 {
     UBYTE ctrl;
 
+    /* Tell the servant to stay off the bus. The Genesis halts this CPU
+     * with SBRQ every frame to read the screen out of PRG-RAM, and a
+     * halt landing inside a CDD exchange stretches it across whole
+     * milliseconds -- far outside the 1/75 s window the gate array is
+     * clocking. A late *read* of the status registers costs nothing,
+     * which is why the passive link was always healthy; a late or
+     * split *command* is exactly the corruption that killed the link
+     * at the first one, on every build, whatever the sequence. No
+     * emulator reproduces it: their arbitration is instant and neither
+     * models the transfer window at all. */
+    *(volatile UWORD *)0xFF8022 |= 0x0008;
+
     /* The VBL is a lower level than this one, so it cannot preempt a
      * handler that keeps being re-entered: if the gate array holds the
      * request asserted, nothing below level 4 ever runs again and the
@@ -405,6 +417,8 @@ void segacd_int_4_c(void)
         cdd_ctrl_ever |= (UBYTE)(*CDD_CTRL_RD & (CDD_DTS | CDD_DRS));
     }
 
+    *(volatile UWORD *)0xFF8022 &= (UWORD)~0x0008;   /* bus is yours */
+
     /* A boolean cannot tell a dead link from a flaky one. Count how
      * many of the last sixteen packets checksummed and report that:
      * F is a clean link, 0 is nothing, anything between is a race. */
